# Shipped assets are bytes, not text. Never normalise their line endings on checkout: espeak-ng
# reads its voice and language files with plain file calls, and a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true (this machine has it) would otherwise check every one of them out with CRLF.
# The food database and the knowledge file are covered by the same rule; binary files are
# unaffected either way.
app/src/main/assets/** -text
